clearcote: battery substitution moves to the dispatcher seam.

150 pinned the four BatteryManager getters to persona constants but left DidUpdateData() reading
the real host status and firing chargingchange/levelchange off real old-vs-new comparisons: on a
laptop a page saw levelchange fire while level stayed 1.0, an event for a value that did not
change. BatteryDispatcher::OnDidChange() now publishes the persona status (four-argument
BatteryStatus ctor, so level takes the same two-digit rounding a host reading takes) and the
getters are upstream again, reading that status. One value, one owner: getters, HasLastData() and
the four events derive from it and nothing can fire. Values in every mode are the ones 150 served.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/battery/battery_dispatcher.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/battery/battery_dispatcher.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,11 @@
 
